THIS FILE IS INERT. IT HALTS NOTHING. (corrected 2026-10-05)

Nothing in the pipeline reads this path. The enrichment chain reads its halt flag
at logs/backfill-2026-07/halt.flag, and scripts/backfill/chain.sh deliberately
warns about this file rather than honouring it, because honouring it would stop
enrichment the moment that code deployed.

What it used to say, and why that was worse than saying nothing:

  migration freeze: the old database -> Postgres cutover in progress (2026-08-12...)
  Remove this file to resume: rm scripts/backfill/halt.flag

Both lines were false by the time anyone read them. The Postgres cutover finished
on 2026-08-12, and removing this file resumes nothing because nothing is stopped.
A reader who found it would conclude enrichment had been frozen for weeks.

TO ACTUALLY STOP ENRICHMENT:
  touch /home/casey/repos/youtube-outreach-orchestrator-v1/logs/backfill-2026-07/halt.flag

TO ACTUALLY STOP THE AUTOPILOT CAMPAIGN LOOP:
  touch /home/casey/repos/youtube-outreach-orchestrator-v1/logs/autopilot-halt.flag

Kept rather than deleted so chain.sh's warning stays exercised against a real
file. Safe to delete.
